<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">Persarmenia</h1><p class="st-meta">428 CE – 646 CE (approx.) · capital Dvin</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Persian-ruled part of Armenia after the end of its monarchy, where Armenians fought to keep their Christian faith and their church took its independent path.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>When the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-armenia-arsacid">Kingdom of Armenia (Arsacid)</a> was abolished in 428, the larger eastern part of the country, assigned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> by the partition of 387, became a province of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a>. It was governed by a marzpan, often an Armenian noble, from the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dvin">Dvin</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Armenian noble houses kept their lands and armies, and the church remained central to society. When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazdegerd-ii">Yazdegerd II</a> tried to impose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zoroastrianism">Zoroastrianism</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vardan-mamikonian">Vardan Mamikonian</a> led a revolt that was crushed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-avarayr">Avarayr</a> in 451 but secured toleration, confirmed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-nvarsak">Treaty of Nvarsak</a> in 484. Councils at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dvin">Dvin</a> rejected <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chalcedon">Chalcedon</a>, separating the Armenian church from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/byzantium">Byzantium</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 591 most of the province was ceded to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/byzantium">Byzantium</a>, and later wars returned it to contest. Arab armies took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dvin">Dvin</a> in 640, and by the 650s the region had become the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-armenia">Principality of Armenia</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/persarmenia.jpg" alt="Persarmenia" width="320" height="208"><figcaption>Image: Armenica.org · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Persian_Armenia.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>428 CE – 646 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Dvin</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Vasak Siuni, Vahan Mamikonian</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Armenian Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Armenian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/armenia">Armenia</a>, <a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a>, <a href="/countries/iran">Iran</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Marzpanate of Armenia, Sasanian Armenia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=537&amp;focus=persarmenia" aria-label="Persarmenia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5777 746 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Persarmenia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6097 1002L6079 1051M6097 1002L6357 1235M6097 1002L6097 1002"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6079 1051h0M6357 1235h0M6097 1002h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6097 1002h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6097 1002h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Dvin. <a href="/atlas?year=537&amp;focus=persarmenia">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
